    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Differentiating between these specific groupings carries significant ethical risks, as authenticity should never rely on essentializing ethnicity into a single \"gang\" stereotype or set of combatant behaviors for a period piece. Instead of seeking predetermined cultural traits for different groups, focus on casting actors from the specific real-world communities of your chosen neighborhood who are navigating the actual socio-economic pressures of 1975 New York. The tension should come from the universal human dynamics of conflict and survival within that era, supported by specific period-accurate mannerisms like the unique delivery of Spanish dialects or the rhythm of Black spoken English, rather than assuming how a person of a certain race \"fights.\" Ultimately, consulting working with the local community through community arts programs ensures a respectful and historically grounded performance that resonates truthfully without relying on harmful generalizations.",
